---
import { SITE } from "../data/site";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Privacy policy (draft)" description="Draft privacy policy for Matrix Eye early access: what we collect on this website, why, and how to ask for your details to be removed." noindex>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <span class="eyebrow">Draft</span>
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>

      <div class="callout callout--draft" role="note">
        <p><strong>Draft, not yet legal advice.</strong> This describes what the website actually does today, in plain language. Items in [square brackets] are decisions still to be made. It must be reviewed by a qualified lawyer, and completed with the operating company's details, before launch.</p>
      </div>

      <p class="meta">Last updated: October 2026 &middot; Applies to this website only. If you run Matrix Eye yourself, your visitors' data stays on your own servers and is governed by your policy, not this one.</p>

      <h2 id="who">Who we are</h2>
      <p>This website is operated by {SITE.legalEntity} ("we", "Matrix Eye"). You can reach us through the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>

      <h2 id="collect">What we collect, and why</h2>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">When</th><th scope="col">What we store</th><th scope="col">Why</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">You join the waitlist</th><td>Your email address, and if you choose to give them: your name, what you would use Matrix Eye for, the page you signed up from, and the time you agreed to be contacted.</td><td>To tell you when early access opens and to learn what people need.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">You send a message</th><td>Your name, email address and message, and the time.</td><td>To reply to you.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">You visit the site</th><td>Our hosting provider keeps standard server logs (such as your IP address, the page and the time) for security and reliability. [Retention period and provider to be named.]</td><td>Keeping the site running and secure.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>We store nothing without your action and agreement: the forms require you to tick a box saying we may contact you.</p>

      <h2 id="cookies">Cookies and tracking</h2>
      <p>This website sets <strong>no cookies</strong> and loads <strong>no third-party scripts, fonts, analytics or advertising trackers</strong>. If you pick the light or dark theme, that choice is remembered in your own browser (local storage) and is never sent to us. [If analytics are added later, this section and a notice will be updated first.]</p>

      <h2 id="sharing">Who we share it with</h2>
      <p>We do not sell your details. [List of service providers that process data on our behalf, such as hosting and email delivery, to be added.]</p>

      <h2 id="keep">How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>[Retention period to be decided, for example: until you ask us to remove you, or a fixed period after the product launches, whichever is sooner.]</p>

      <h2 id="rights">Your rights</h2>
      <p>You can ask to see what we hold about you, to correct it, or to have it erased, and you can withdraw your agreement to be contacted at any time. Send a request through the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> from the email address concerned; we can find and erase waitlist and contact records for an address and will confirm when done. [Local rights, such as those under GDPR or other privacy laws, and the supervisory authority to contact, to be added with legal advice.]</p>

      <h2 id="children">Children</h2>
      <p>Matrix Eye is for businesses and developers and is not directed at children.</p>

      <h2 id="changes">Changes</h2>
      <p>We will update this page when what we do changes, and show the date above. For significant changes affecting people on the waitlist we will email them.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
